          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The line segment from <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 0]</span> to <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 1]</span> is split into <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\color{blue}6]</span> equal parts. Each part represents <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}6}]</span> of a whole.</p><div class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/1cf32f123e3f1f58047b7226300ad5f1\"></div><p>Starting from zero, we land on our point by making <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\color{red}2]</span> whole steps plus <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\color{blue}1]</span> part step:</p><div class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/94e3752ec43416082cc2e879baa027fc\"></div><p>Therefore, the mixed number is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{red}2}{\\color{blue}\\dfrac{1}{6}}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The line segment from [MATH: 0] to [MATH: 1] is split into [MATH: \\color{blue}6] equal parts. Each part represents [MATH: \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}6}] of a whole.\n\n[IMG: /graphics/1cf32f123e3f1f58047b7226300ad5f1]\n\nStarting from zero, we land on our point by making [MATH: \\color{red}2] whole steps plus [MATH: \\color{blue}1] part step:\n\n[IMG: /graphics/94e3752ec43416082cc2e879baa027fc]\n\nTherefore, the mixed number is [MATH: {\\color{red}2}{\\color{blue}\\dfrac{1}{6}}.]",
